.policy "ruff-f634-if-tuple" revision 3
.description "Don't use a tuple as an if or elif condition; a non-empty tuple is always true, so the branch always runs."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff F634 (pyflakes): an `if` or `elif` whose test is a non-empty tuple, which is always true. Reported at the
// test.
//   if (a, b): ...           ← F634
//   elif (c,): ...           ← F634
//   if (): ...               not reported: the empty tuple is false
#include "python/pyflakes.rr"
//   nonempty_tuple(e)  e, through parentheses, is a tuple with at least one element

.violation F634(at: node) code "F634"
    "Replace this tuple condition with the intended boolean expression; a non-empty tuple is always true."
    suppress ruff "F634"
F634(t) :- py_if(_, t, _), nonempty_tuple(t).
